# 🖋️ Deep Learning: Handwritten Digit Recognizer

A high-accuracy Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) built to recognize handwritten digits in real-time. This project demonstrates an end-to-end Machine Learning pipeline: from **data augmentation** and **model training** in Google Colab to a **live web dashboard** via Streamlit.



## 🚀 Features
* **99%+ Accuracy:** Trained on a Deep CNN with Batch Normalization and Dropout to minimize confusion between digits like 1 and 7.
* **Real-time Canvas:** Interactive drawing board for user input.
* **Auto-Centering Logic:** Pre-processing that crops and centers drawings to match the AI's training data.
* **Founder-Ready Architecture:** Clean, modular code designed for scalability.

---

## 🛠️ Local Setup Instructions

Follow these steps to run the project on your local machine:

### 1. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/HammadFarooqi/Task_3_Handwritten_Digit_Recognition.git](https://github.com/HammadFarooqi/Task_3_Handwritten_Digit_Recognition.git)
cd Task_3_Handwritten_Digit_Recognition


HOW TO RUN 

python -m venv venv_final
.\venv_final\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py